solutionSteps.body:
$$\begin{aligned}
k_{t+1}&=\frac{K_{t+1}}{H_{t+1}}
=\frac{(1-\delta)K_t+I_t}{(1+n)H_t},\\
&=\frac{(1-\delta)k_t+i_t}{1+n}.
\end{aligned}$$

The numerator combines surviving capital and new investment per current worker; the denominator spreads it over the larger next-period workforce. This distinction is why a discrete-time law contains the gross labour-growth factor rather than simply subtracting $n$ without derivation.
